# Auto-commit after every change

After making any file changes in this repository, always `git add` the relevant files and create a git commit before ending the turn.

Follow the project's committing-changes protocol (status/diff/log, HEREDOC commit message, no force push, no config changes, no secrets). Treat this preference as an explicit standing request to commit — do not wait for the user to ask again.

Skip the commit only when there is nothing to commit, or when the user explicitly says not to commit for a specific change.
